WEBVTT

00:06:29.281 --> 00:06:32.568
is that everybody in this room
could live an extra 5, 10, 20 years,

00:06:32.592 --> 00:06:34.259
just because of this one thing.

00:06:34.283 --> 00:06:36.346
Which is a fantastic story,

00:06:36.370 --> 00:06:39.248
unless you think about
humanity's footprint on the planet,

00:06:39.272 --> 00:06:41.747
and our ability to keep up
food production.

00:06:41.771 --> 00:06:43.343
So it turns out

00:06:43.367 --> 00:06:47.308
that the very same technology
is also being used to grow new lines

00:06:47.332 --> 00:06:50.461
of corn, wheat, soybean and other crops

00:06:50.485 --> 00:06:52.660
that are highly tolerant
of drought, of flood,

00:06:52.684 --> 00:06:54.207
of pests and pesticides.

00:06:54.231 --> 00:06:55.405
Now, look --

00:06:55.924 --> 00:06:58.298
as long as we continue
to increase the population,

00:06:58.322 --> 00:07:01.501
we'll have to continue to grow and eat
genetically modified foods.